% ---------- About ----------
\cvsection{About}
AI builder and MS Data Science candidate at the University of Edinburgh. Solo-shipped \textbf{LingoTrack}, an iOS vocabulary trainer for Mandarin learners with \textbf{800+ paying subscribers}, acquired through a self-built \textbf{8K-subscriber} newsletter on computational linguistics. Open-sourced an MLOps experiment-tracking library (\textbf{1.2K GitHub stars}). Seeking ML Engineer or Data-leaning Founder Associate roles at UK AI startups; UK Graduate Visa eligible, no sponsorship required.

% ---------- Projects ----------
\cvsection{Projects}

\noindent\textbf{LingoTrack — iOS vocabulary trainer} \,---\, Founder \& Sole Developer \hfill \textit{2025 -- Present}\\
\href{https://example.com/lingotrack}{Live on UK App Store} \,\textbar\, iOS / Swift, SwiftUI, Core Data, OpenAI API
\begin{itemize}
  \item Built and launched an iOS app for spaced-repetition vocabulary practice with adaptive AI-generated example sentences for Mandarin learners.
  \item Grew to \textbf{800+ paying subscribers} ($\pounds$3.99 / mo) through an \textbf{8K-subscriber newsletter} on computational linguistics; owned product, growth, support, and App Store operations.
  \item Designed difficulty progression around forgetting curves rather than fixed schedules, differentiating from Anki / Quizlet on adaptive scheduling.
\end{itemize}

\noindent\textbf{mlops-track — Open Source experiment tracking, MIT} \hfill \textit{2025}\\
\href{https://github.com/alexchen-example/mlops-track}{github.com/alexchen-example/mlops-track} \,\textbar\, Python, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Docker
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{1.2K GitHub stars}, used by 40+ research labs and small ML teams; lightweight alternative to MLflow / Weights\&Biases for solo researchers.
  \item Designed for offline-first workflows: SQLite local storage, optional Postgres sync, no cloud dependency. Documentation, examples, CI / CD all maintained solo.
\end{itemize}

\noindent\textbf{compling.dev — Newsletter on computational linguistics} \,---\, Founder \hfill \textit{2024 -- Present}\\
\href{https://compling.dev}{compling.dev} \,\textbar\, Substack, weekly cadence
\begin{itemize}
  \item Grew from zero to \textbf{8{,}000 subscribers} in 18 months through long-form writing on tokenization, embedding intuitions, and small-team ML practice.
  \item Primary acquisition channel for LingoTrack; converted $\sim$10\% of newsletter readers to paid app subscribers (verified via UTM-tagged in-app links).
\end{itemize}

